{"id":"d4d317c47fe1ba6e","group":"58","path":"58/batch10/58-df-nuclear-operator.md","title":"Nuclear Operator","display":"df-nuclear-operator — Nuclear Operator","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-nuclear-operator","aliases":["58-df-nuclear-operator"],"display":"df-nuclear-operator — Nuclear Operator","depends_on":["[[../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-nuclear-operator"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-nuclear-operator</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-nuclear-operator — Nuclear Operator"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"e824a8435bba9f97\" href=\"?note=e824a8435bba9f97\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md\">../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2\\in V\">\\(T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> is the Hilbert-space nuclear-norm predicate from <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"e824a8435bba9f97\" href=\"?note=e824a8435bba9f97\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md\">../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NuclearOperator}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{NuclearOperator}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}nuclear\\text{-}operator}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{NuclearOperator}_S\n(T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\n\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S\n(r,T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}nuclear\\text{-}operator}\\vdash{}&amp;\n\\mathrm{NuclearOperator}_S\n(T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&amp;\n\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\n\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S\n(r,T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Finiteness is enforced by <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\">\\(r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\)</span>, while the upstream singular-value sum may otherwise take the value <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"+\\infty\">\\(+\\infty\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The earlier three-place formulation invoked a bounded-linear predicate with the wrong arity and duplicated an untyped tensor-series definition of the nuclear norm.</li>\n<li>Between Hilbert spaces these are exactly the trace-class operators.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md","status":"resolved","id":"e824a8435bba9f97","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md","status":"resolved","id":"e824a8435bba9f97","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ is the Hilbert-space nuclear-norm predicate from [[../batch09/58-df-nuclear-norm.md]].","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S:V^6\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NuclearOperator}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{df\\text{-}nuclear\\text{-}operator}\\vdash{}&\n\\mathrm{NuclearOperator}_S\n(T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2)\\\\\n\\leftrightarrow{}&\n\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\n\\mathrm{NuclearNorm}_S\n(r,T,H_1,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_1,H_2,\\langle\\cdot,\\cdot\\rangle_2).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"r\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}","display":false},{"tex":"+\\infty","display":false}],"bytes":1288,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-893","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch10/58-df-nuclear-operator.md|58-df-nuclear-operator]]（batch10）"}],"outgoing":["e824a8435bba9f97"]}